# A large walkable slope passes above a small buried obstacle shell. The
# obstacle probe lies near the high side of the polygon, where the local
# surface is much higher than the polygon's vertex-average height. Semantic
# verification must sample the polygon at the probe instead of comparing the
# obstacle against that unrelated average.
o sloped_terrain
v 0 0 0
v 12 6 0
v 12 6 10
v 0 0 10
usemtl nav_terrain
f 1 4 3
f 1 3 2

# This box is entirely below the terrain around x=9 (terrain y=4.5). Its
# horizontal faces remain valid obstacle probes, but they must not invalidate
# the distinct walkable surface above them.
o buried_boulder_shell
v 8.8 3.8 4.8
v 9.2 3.8 4.8
v 9.2 3.8 5.2
v 8.8 3.8 5.2
v 8.8 4.0 4.8
v 9.2 4.0 4.8
v 9.2 4.0 5.2
v 8.8 4.0 5.2
usemtl nav_obstacle_static
f 5 6 7
f 5 7 8
f 9 12 11
f 9 11 10
f 5 9 10
f 5 10 6
f 6 10 11
f 6 11 7
f 7 11 12
f 7 12 8
f 8 12 9
f 8 9 5
